.TH L10N-LINT 1 "September 2026" "l10n-lint 1.20.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
l10n-lint \- linter for localization files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B l10n-lint
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIPATH\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B l10n-lint
checks gettext .po and Qt .ts localization files for common issues.
Supports local files, directories, URLs, and GitHub repositories.
.SH CHECKS
.SS Core
missing-translation, fuzzy, placeholder-mismatch, duplicate
.SS Typography
inconsistent-punctuation, inconsistent-capitalization, trailing-whitespace,
double-spaces, mixed-quotes
.SS Technical
html-tag-mismatch, escaped-chars-mismatch, keyboard-shortcut-missing,
nordic-accelerator, numeric-mismatch
.SS Quality
untranslated-words, repeated-words, source-equals-translation, suspicious-length
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version number and exit.
.TP
.BR \-G ", " \-\-gtk
Launch the GTK graphical interface. Can optionally be followed by file paths.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-github " " \fIREPO\fR
Lint a GitHub repository (owner/repo or URL).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format: text (default), json, github
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Show only summary line.
.TP
.BR \-\-check
Exit code only, no output (for CI).
.TP
.BR \-\-skip\-fuzzy
Ignore fuzzy warnings.
.TP
.BR \-\-strict
Treat warnings as errors.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B l10n-lint ./translations/
Lint all .po and .ts files in the translations directory.
.TP
.B l10n-lint https://example.com/locale/sv.po
Lint a file from a URL.
.TP
.B l10n-lint \-\-github owner/repo
Lint all localization files in a GitHub repository.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No issues found.
.TP
.B 1
Issues found or error occurred.
.SH AUTHOR
Daniel Nylander <daniel@danielnylander.se>
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tp-lint (1),
.BR po-translate (1)

.SH PROJECT WORKFLOWS
The nearest pyproject.toml in the current directory or its ancestors can define
[tool.l10n-lint]. CLI arguments override project defaults. Configuration paths
are relative to the TOML file.
.TP
.BI --config " FILE"
Read project settings from FILE.
.TP
.B --list-rules
List diagnostic IDs, severities and language scopes.
.TP
.BI --language " LOCALE"
Override the target language used by language-specific checks.
.TP
.BI --exclude " GLOB"
Exclude a project-relative glob. Repeat to supply multiple patterns.
.TP
.BI --baseline " FILE"
Report only findings absent from a versioned JSON baseline. Operational errors
cannot be suppressed.
.TP
.BI --write-baseline " FILE"
Save current findings before filtering. Retains the ordinary lint exit status.
.TP
.BI --reference " FILE"
Compare entries with a .pot/.po or source .ts catalog of the same format.
.TP
.BI --fix " whitespace,ellipsis"
Preview conservative local UTF-8 PO translation fixes as a unified diff on stderr.
.TP
.B --apply
Apply the fixes selected by --fix, then lint the updated files.
.TP
.BI --format " sarif"
Emit a SARIF 2.1.0 report suitable for code scanning.
.TP
.BI --length-ratio " NUMBER"
Set the maximum recommended translation/source length ratio (default 3).
.TP
.BI --max-errors " NUMBER"
Allow this many lint errors before failing (default 0). Operational errors always fail.
.TP
.BI --max-warnings " NUMBER"
Allow this many warnings before failing (default 0).
.PP
Exit status is 0 within thresholds, 1 for excess warnings, or 2 for excess errors
or operational failures. With --strict, excess warnings return 2. Informational
findings do not fail the run. See README.md for configuration examples and limits.
